        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#eef4fb;font-family:system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#182d4c'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:6px solid #294b83;border-bottom:1px solid #182d4c;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>TWILITE ZONE · TEMPLATES</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:850 clamp(36px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.035em;text-wrap:balance;color:#182d4c'>What a canon template is</h1></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;flex-direction:row-reverse;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #182d4c'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#182d4c'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #a6bed9'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Status</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>Approved 2026-10-21. Rule 14 added 2026-11-03. Each rule is short, says why, and says how it is checked: twelve can be checked mechanically, and two are judgement.</dd></dl></section></div><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>What it is</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A <strong>canon template</strong> is a starter graph in the Twilite Zone library (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>library/templates/&lt;name&gt;/</code>) that other graphs are made from, and that follows these rules.</p></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>1. One surface, three looks</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A canon template presents through one Surface: a Detail, then a Summary, then a Glyph. An Icon view is optional. Add one when the template benefits from it (the Person Profile&#39;s face is an example), and leave it off when it doesn&#39;t.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* The glyph is the floor: it stands for the graph at small sizes and hands over to the lowest view once that view can be read.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>2. One shape</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The Detail defines the graph&#39;s shape, and the views behind it take it. Each view&#39;s own size says when it appears: the Summary is smaller than the Detail and appears sooner.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* Views that share a shape look the same in a workspace tile, a portal and the graph itself, whatever the zoom.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* faceShapeIssues (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>3. Derived, not typed</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The Detail, the Summary and the Glyph are written by the template&#39;s own Method, which a graph.changed event runs through an invokes edge. There is no stored summary node and no copy that is kept in step by hand. The saved file holds the current views.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A summary that is typed goes stale, and a stale one is worse than none.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test: the stored views equal what the Method derives (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>4. Each look is the graph at that size</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The Glyph says what kind of thing the graph is, and carries its state if it has one. The Summary is the graph in miniature. The Detail is the graph. If graphs of this template have a state someone has to act on (for example the status of a task, or an open question), it is shown on every look, so no one has to open the graph to find out whether they need to.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A look should answer the question its size can answer. The state rule applies only to templates that have a state.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Judgement; each look and each state is a case in the tests of the template itself.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>5. A view fits its page, or is one page that scrolls</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A view is measured from its own width (cqw inside an outer container, never on the container itself) and is one of two things. A <strong>card</strong> fits its fixed page and says how many more when there is more than fits. A <strong>page</strong> is one scrolling area, the whole view, which the workspace can scroll at every size by the wheel, the thumb and the track. A scrolling area nested inside a fixed card is not allowed for now, because the workspace cannot carry it yet; that can change if a template needs one.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* The app already scrolls a page view at every size and moves the nodes with it. It cannot yet scroll a region inside a card, so a card that needed one would show a scrollbar nobody could use.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test: a card has no scrolling area, a long list still fits, and a page has exactly one (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>6. A window of its own shape</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The graph&#39;s window (the root&#39;s membrane bounds) is authored in the Detail&#39;s shape and holds everything the graph has.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A new graph is the size of a graph, and its Detail fills it without stretching.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>7. Pieces are classes, and relationships have names</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Each kind of thing in the template is a node class, imported through a Bridge, and each node carries the class&#39;s ports. Relationships are edge classes between named ports (precedes leaves next and arrives at previous). Nothing is drawn by side, and nothing depends on one particular edge being present: deleting an edge changes how the graph is drawn, not what it says.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* Names say what a connection means; sides do not.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>8. One export</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The template hands on its classes and its Method through a single export with an allowlist. A graph made from it imports once.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* One Bridge is a thing to read; ten are a thing to maintain.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>9. Canon addresses, and an identity of its own</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Everything the template points at is a canon address (tlz://twilite.zone/...) and nothing personal. A copy gets its own graph id and node ids.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* Canon has to stand on its own, and copies must not be drawn as one node.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>10. Events run through edges</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A Method runs only through an invokes edge from an event port to a Method in the same graph. There are no Event Handler nodes.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* One model for events; this is already the rule everywhere.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* The validator (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>11. Generic, complete starter content</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The template shows each state it can be in, with placeholder content and nobody&#39;s real work. Its landing page says what it is, what it derives and what it exports.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A starter is copied; real work in it is a mistake waiting to be copied.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Judgement; read at approval.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>12. It is tested</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A canon template has tests for the rules above, so it cannot drift: a valid graph, the shape, the stored views, each state, and a long list.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* The standard is only a standard if breaking it fails.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* The audit in tests/helpers/templateStandard.js runs the mechanical rules over every template.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>13. An environment</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A canon template has an environment: a face of its own on an <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>environment</code> edge from the root, the backdrop its interior sits on. It is never the Detail, the Summary or the Glyph.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A graph&#39;s interior is the room its work happens in. A template that sets none leaves every graph made from it on whatever backdrop the app falls back to, so it cannot say what kind of room this is.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>14. Where it asks, it has a place to answer</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Where a template expects input, the form gives a labelled place for it, near where it is needed, and the card shows what is missing. Every text a card shows has a field for it; a list of short texts is typed one to a line, never as JSON; and what is waiting on a person (an answer, a reason) says so on the card until it is filled in.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Why:* A starter that asks a question but has nowhere to answer it leaves the person guessing which field to misuse, and a card that never says it is waiting is easy to ignore.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>*Checked by:* Test: every text a card of the template&#39;s classes shows has a field in its form, and none of those fields is raw JSON (mechanical). That the card says what is missing is judgement; read at approval.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #182d4c'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:750 22px/1.1 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#182d4c'>Templates</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#46617f'>The canon templates.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#46617f'>Open the templates →</a></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>What it is not</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>It is not a demo with someone&#39;s real work in it, not a copy of a primitives page, and not two templates folded into one: the plan template and the Task Template stay separate.</p></section></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
