    {
      "id": "canon-standard-section-15",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "14. Where it asks, it has a place to answer",
      "position": {
        "x": 810,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "14. Where it asks, it has a place to answer",
        "body": "Where a template expects input, the form gives a labelled place for it, near where it is needed, and the card shows what is missing. Every text a card shows has a field for it; a list of short texts is typed one to a line, never as JSON; and what is waiting on a person (an answer, a reason) says so on the card until it is filled in.\n\n*Why:* A starter that asks a question but has nowhere to answer it leaves the person guessing which field to misuse, and a card that never says it is waiting is easy to ignore.\n\n*Checked by:* Test: every text a card of the template's classes shows has a field in its form, and none of those fields is raw JSON (mechanical). That the card says what is missing is judgement; read at approval.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-standard"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
